# .dockerignore — controls what is sent to the Docker daemon as build context.
# Keep build context lean: exclude data stores, binaries, and repo metadata that
# have no place in any image layer.

# ── Version control ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Git history and metadata are never needed inside an image.
.git/
.gitignore

# ── Beads / Dolt data store ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .beads/ holds the local Dolt database and task state. It can be large and
# must never be baked into an image.
.beads/

# ── Compiled binaries (Windows) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Windows .exe builds produced by local `go build` runs. The Dockerfiles do
# their own Go builds (or COPY a pre-built Linux binary) — Windows artefacts
# are irrelevant and can be several MB each.
*.exe

# ── Compiled binaries (Linux, built locally) ──────────────────────────────────
# If a developer runs `go build ./cmd/archon` locally they produce a bare
# `archon` binary. Same for the `lg` helper. Exclude them so they don't shadow
# anything inside the image.
# NOTE: `vessel-driver` is intentionally NOT listed here — Dockerfile.vessel-copilot
#       does `COPY vessel-driver /usr/local/bin/vessel-driver` and requires it
#       to be present in the build context.
archon
lg

# ── Test artefacts ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.test
*.out
tests/

# ── CI / GitHub metadata ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.github/

# ── Archive / docs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Historical notes and stack design docs; not needed at build time.
archive/
README.md
